id: schemas/node
title: "schema modules"
kind: schema-index
status: active
updated: 2026-08-14

purpose: >
  Hold machine-valid state-substrate modules and explicitly labeled protocol
  drafts. Each schema is canonical only for its own version and kind.

holds:
  - statuses.v1.schema.json
  - event.v1.schema.json
  - materialized-state.v1.schema.json
  - state-snapshot.v1.schema.json
  - desire.v1.schema.json
  - target-condition.v1.schema.json
  - transition-intent.v1.schema.json
  - transition-result.v1.schema.json
  - state-update.v1.schema.json
  - living-snapshot.v1.schema.json
  - agency-holarchy.v0.2.schema.json
  - orientation-passage.v1.schema.json
  - public-view.v1.schema.json

compatibility: >
  Legacy current/possible/desired fields remain readable at system boundaries.
  Canonical V1 records use attributed snapshots, optional targets, explicit
  authority, and separate transition intent/result.

module_boundary: >
  The @yawn/contracts package is the stable v1 constitution/runtime bundle.
  These root schemas are the parallel state-substrate v1 modules plus the
  experimental Agency Holarchy 0.2 aggregate. Neither surface is described as
  the complete schema for every human-readable .yawn file.

agency_holarchy_draft: >
  Draft 0.2 adds provider-neutral arena boundaries, one-parent holarchy,
  lateral relations, asynchronous turns, transitions, proof receipts, routing
  proposals, and structural-change receipts without redefining v1.

orientation_passage_contract: >
  Orientation Passage V1 keeps acquisition, statement, Orientation, Choice,
  Intention, outward Projection, Move, Consequence, authority, and Proof
  separately addressable.

public_view_contract: >
  Public View V1 is a deterministic, public-safe rendering contract. Its
  snapshot hash covers semantic content, never layout, media, QR rendering, or
  agent overlay state.

status_rule: >
  Modal, motivational, epistemic, lifecycle, authority, loop,
  axis-resolution, and presentation statuses are independent dimensions.

proof:
  command: "npm ci && npm test"
  status: contract-defined
